Z||000003||william_thorniii||05-08-2000||01:55 AM||||Paul,<P>She is a beaut!  The important thing is that with this ride, beauty is more than skin deep.  With the Quad 4 breathing fire in her mid-section and the 88 suspension keeping her planted down, I am certain that this will be one impressive ride.  Just my style (except the color... too much attention for a young guy like myself).  <P>On a side note, I really did enjoy speaking with you at the swap meet.  It was so great to put some names with faces.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000004||pherder||05-08-2000||07:59 AM||||Actually, I will be putting the stock lights back on this car.<P>I will use the lightweight lights on my Formula race car.<P>After seeing George Ryan's gutted 84 Fiero race car @ the swap meet, I plan to gut my Formula, put my Ryane Motorsports' front tubular control arms and coil overs and lower the suspension, and put in a V8.  I will have a 16 gal. fuel cell in front with the battery and will get rid of the extra metal/plastic that isn't needed.<P>And Ozzy, reread the first line, it will answer your questions on the lights.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||1
