Z||000009||pherder||05-10-2000||06:36 PM||||One thing everyone should know BEFORE they jump on the Quad 4 wagon ...<P>They have a "problem" with their head gaskets ... STOCK!  To add a turbo or supercharger will just quicken the death of the engine.<P>There are two kinds of people who own Quad 4 engines ... those who have had to change out the head gasket and those who will ...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>Now ... EVERYONE read the first line ... I will wait ... Have you read it? ... the car doesn't run yet!!!  I have no idea, nada, how fast it is or whether my wiring harness or the ECM and PROM will work together!<P>93 engine and sensors<BR>89 wiring harness<BR>90 PROM for (I hope) a HO Quad 4 5 speed.<BR>97 Sunfire Isuzu 5 speed w/3.83:1 FDR<P>I have the 93 ECM but could not get the 93 harness (cut up @ the salvage yard).  Had a 88-91 ECM and a 89 wiring harness from an automatic quad 4.  Merged the Fiero's engine compartment wiring harness with the 89 Quad 4 engine compartment harness and made the modifications to make it work with the 5 speed (I hope).<P>I did what EVERYONE is told NOT to do!  Get bits and pieces from several donor cars.  To do this right (and less costly) EVERYTHING should come from ONE DONER!<P>Well one thing I have in my favor ... if it doesn't run or perform like I want it to ... I can always put the 350 TPI V8 in it ... I do have Archie's kit and a spare 88 cradle, suspension, brakes, 2 spare transaxles, and a set of remanufactured axles.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||1
